From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:05:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: the PCIe0 WAKE#
 line is active low

With GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH the wake GPIO (TLMM 104, pulled up, pinctrl state wake-n) reads active all the time, so
the root port dedicated wake IRQ fires as soon as the system enters s2idle: on the OnePlus Pad 4 every suspend
with Wi-Fi enabled returned within a second with pm_wakeup_irq = 0000:00:00.0:wakeup, and slept for the full RTC
alarm once that wakeup was disabled. PCIe WAKE# is an active-low open-drain signal.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 16066d23d8f3..bd4fc183fbc6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1225,7 +1225,7 @@
 };
 
 &pcie_port0 {
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	wifi@0 {
